        <h2 id="s1">1. Introduction and acceptance</h2>
        <p>These Terms of Use (the "Terms") govern your use of the Matdo Grade application for iPhone and iPad (the "App"), published by Matdo Lab LLC ("Matdo", "we", "us", "our"). By downloading, installing or using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree to them, do not use the App. If you are agreeing on behalf of a school, tutoring centre or other organisation, you confirm that you have authority to bind it, and "you" means both you and it. How the App handles personal information is described separately in our Privacy Policy, which forms part of these Terms. The current version of these Terms is also published at <a href="https://matdolab.com/grade/terms">matdolab.com/grade/terms</a>.</p>
        <h2 id="s2">2. Summary</h2>
        <p>Non-binding summary:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Matdo Grade marks photographed pages with an AI model and shows you the result.</li>
          <li>It is a marking aid. The model can be wrong, and every mark is yours to check before you act on it.</li>
          <li>Grading needs the internet: pages are sent to our service and on to Google's Gemini model on Google Cloud, and the reply comes back.</li>
          <li>We keep no copy of any page or any grade.</li>
          <li>Grading is charged in units: 10 for a page the grade marks at Brief output, 30 at Detailed, and 5 for a page the model only reads. A grade that comes back empty or cut off costs nothing.</li>
          <li>New users get a one-time grant of free units; after it is spent, grading needs a monthly subscription or a top-up. Nothing here is unlimited.</li>
          <li>Apple processes every purchase, renewal and refund. We never see payment details.</li>
          <li>The App is provided as-is.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This summary is for clarity only; where it differs from the numbered sections, those sections prevail.</p>
        <h2 id="s3">3. Definitions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>App</strong>: The Matdo Grade application for iPhone and iPad, including any update or new version we make available through the App Store.</li>
          <li><strong>Service</strong>: The grading service we operate, which relays a grading request to the grading model and returns the reply.</li>
          <li><strong>Student Work</strong>: The pages you capture and submit for grading, together with anything written on them, and the grades, annotations and feedback the App produces from them.</li>
          <li><strong>Output</strong>: What the model returns for a page: marks, answers, worked solutions, rubric verdicts and written feedback.</li>
          <li><strong>Device</strong>: The iPhone or iPad on which the App is installed.</li>
          <li><strong>Output Level</strong>: Brief, which returns each mark with the student's answer, the correct answer and a one-line working check; or Detailed, which adds worked solutions and notes on where the working appears to go wrong.</li>
          <li><strong>Unit</strong>: The measure in which grading is charged, set out in section 12.</li>
          <li><strong>Allowance</strong>: The Units a Subscription makes available in a calendar month.</li>
          <li><strong>Subscription</strong>: One of the auto-renewing plans sold through the App Store — Lite, Plus, Pro or Max — each providing an Allowance.</li>
          <li><strong>Top-Up</strong>: A one-off purchase of Units that does not renew and does not expire.</li>
          <li><strong>Apple</strong>: Apple Inc. and its subsidiaries, which distribute the App and process every purchase made through the App Store.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 id="s4">4. What Matdo Grade is</h2>
        <p>Matdo Grade captures pages of student work, submits them for grading, and draws the resulting marks onto the page. At Detailed output it also produces worked solutions and notes on where a student's working appears to go wrong, and in Essay Mode it produces rubric verdicts and written feedback. Results are saved on your Device and can be exported as images.</p>
        <p>It is an aid to a teacher's marking, not a replacement for it, and not an assessment or examination service. Independence: Matdo Grade is an independent product. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or connected to Google, Apple, any school, examination board, curriculum authority or franchise brand, and none of them has reviewed or approved it. Every trade mark remains the property of its owner.</p>
        <h2 id="s5">5. The Output is not authoritative, and you must review it</h2>
        <p>This is the most important term in this document. Please read it.</p>
        <p>The App grades with a large language model. Such models misread handwriting, mistake one question for another, apply a method the class was not taught, state a correct working and then a wrong final answer, and occasionally invent something that is not on the page at all. The App contains checks for several of these failures and flags what it catches, but it cannot catch them all, and a wrong mark is often stated as confidently as a right one.</p>
        <p>Accordingly: the Output is a draft for your review, and nothing more. You must check it before returning a mark to a student, entering it in a gradebook, reporting it to a parent, or relying on it in any decision about a student. Do not use the Output as the sole basis for a grade of record, a placement or streaming decision, a report card, a qualification, a disciplinary or academic-integrity finding, or any other decision with a material effect on a person. You remain the teacher; the judgement stays yours.</p>
        <p>We make no representation that the Output is accurate, complete, pedagogically appropriate or suited to your curriculum, and to the maximum extent permitted by law we are not responsible for a decision made from it.</p>
        <h2 id="s6">6. Apple's role, and which terms prevail</h2>
        <p>The App is distributed through the App Store and licensed to you under Apple's Licensed Application End User License Agreement (the "Apple EULA"). These Terms supplement the Apple EULA; they do not replace it. Where a provision of these Terms conflicts with the Apple EULA, or with the App Store terms applicable to your purchase, those Apple terms prevail to the extent of the conflict and the remainder of these Terms continues in force. These Terms are between you and us alone. Accordingly:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Apple is not a party to these Terms and has no obligation to furnish maintenance or support for the App.</li>
          <li>Apple gives no warranty in respect of the App. In the event of any failure of the App to conform to an applicable warranty, you may notify Apple, and Apple may refund the purchase price; to the maximum extent permitted by law, Apple has no other warranty obligation whatsoever in respect of the App.</li>
          <li>We, not Apple, are responsible for addressing any claim relating to the App, including product liability claims, claims that the App fails to conform to a legal or regulatory requirement, and claims arising under consumer protection or similar legislation.</li>
          <li>We, not Apple, are responsible for the investigation, defence, settlement and discharge of any third-party claim that the App infringes that third party's intellectual property rights.</li>
          <li>You represent that you are not located in a country subject to a United States government embargo or designated as a "terrorist supporting" country, and that you are not on any United States government list of prohibited or restricted parties.</li>
          <li>Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 id="s7">7. Licence</h2>
        <p>Subject to these Terms, we grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the App on Apple-branded devices that you own or control, as permitted by the App Store Usage Rules. A Subscription and its balance belong to one Apple Account, not to one school: every Device signed in to that Apple Account shares them, and a centre that uses several Apple Accounts needs a Subscription for each. Subscriptions and Top-Ups are not shared through Family Sharing. Nothing in this section transfers ownership of the App to you; what you acquire is a licence to use it.</p>
        <h2 id="s8">8. Grading requires a connection to our Service</h2>
        <p>Grading is not performed on your Device. When you tap Grade, the App sends the captured pages to our Service, which relays them to Google's Gemini model on Google Cloud's Vertex AI and returns the reply. Without a working internet connection the App cannot grade, though previously saved grades remain readable offline.</p>
        <p>Google's model is a third-party service we rely on. Its availability, its response times and its behaviour are outside our control, and a change Google makes to it may change the Output or interrupt grading without notice to us. We may change which model or provider we use where that improves or preserves the service.</p>
        <h2 id="s9">9. Permitted use and restrictions</h2>
        <p>You may use the App to grade work submitted to you as a teacher, tutor, parent, or in an equivalent role. You may not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Submit material you have no right to submit, or that you are prohibited from disclosing to a third-party service.</li>
          <li>Use the App to grade work in a context where a student has been told the work will be marked by a human only, without correcting that.</li>
          <li>Copy, modify, translate or create derivative works of the App, except as permitted by law that cannot be excluded by agreement.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the App, or attempt to derive its source code, except to the extent applicable law expressly permits it despite this restriction.</li>
          <li>Rent, lease, lend, sell, sublicense or otherwise transfer the App or your licence, or make it available to any third party as a service.</li>
          <li>Circumvent, disable or interfere with unit accounting, the subscription check, App Check or any other technical measure, or use the App with any tool designed to do so.</li>
          <li>Submit requests automatically, in bulk, or at a volume beyond ordinary classroom use, or use the App as a general interface to the underlying model for anything other than grading.</li>
          <li>Remove or obscure any proprietary notice in the App.</li>
          <li>Use the App unlawfully.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To protect the Service, we apply a daily limit on how many Units one account can spend, set well above ordinary classroom use. A grade that would pass it is declined, not charged, and grading resumes the next day (UTC).</p>
        <h2 id="s10">10. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>Because the App sends work you are entrusted with to a third-party service, several things sit with you and cannot sit with us:</p>
        <p>Permission to submit the work. Confirming that submitting a student's work for AI grading is permitted by your school's policies, your employer, your local law, and any parent or student agreement is your responsibility, not ours. We do not review those obligations and make no representation that the App satisfies them. Obtain any clearance you need before you grade.</p>
        <p>Reviewing the Output. Section 5 applies to every page you grade.</p>
        <p>Your records. Saved grades live only on your Device. Keeping the Device backed up, and exporting anything you must keep, is your responsibility. We hold no copy and can restore nothing.</p>
        <p>The Device. Protecting it with a passcode, keeping its operating system current, and controlling physical access to it are your responsibility, as is where you send an exported page.</p>
        <h2 id="s11">11. Student Work and privacy</h2>
        <p>As between you and us, you (or the school or centre you act for) decide what Student Work is submitted and on what basis. We process it only to return the Output you requested, on your instruction, and for no purpose of our own. We retain no copy of a page or a grade, and we do not use Student Work to train any model. Full detail is in the Privacy Policy, which forms part of these Terms.</p>
        <h2 id="s12">12. Units, and the free grant</h2>
        <p>Grading is charged in Units. A page the grade puts marks on costs 10 Units at Brief output and 30 Units at Detailed output. A page the model only reads in order to grade another — an article, a passage, a question sheet — costs 5 at either level; you can tag such a page as a context page before grading. Your balance, and which balance it is drawn from, are shown in Settings. Page counts shown in the App assume a typical marked page at Brief output.</p>
        <p>Units are charged after the grade comes back and according to what the grade did, not to what you uploaded. A grade that returns no graded work, and a grade the Service cuts off because the reply ran past its length limit, are charged nothing. Before grading, the App checks that your balance could cover every page as a marked page at the chosen Output Level; if it cannot, the grade does not start. Re-grading a page — including at a different Output Level, or after switching between Worksheet and Essay mode — is a new grade and is charged again.</p>
        <p>The App includes a one-time grant of free Units, currently 100, or about ten marked pages at Brief output. It is granted once per Apple Account and does not reset: it is a trial, not a recurring monthly allowance. When it is spent, grading needs a Subscription or a Top-Up. Saved grades stay readable either way, and the history, export and rubric editor keep working with an empty balance.</p>
        <p>We may change the Unit cost of a page, or the size of the free grant, for the future. A change does not retroactively re-charge a grade you have already been given, and it does not reduce a balance you have already bought.</p>
        <h2 id="s13">13. Subscriptions, Top-Ups, renewal, and cancellation</h2>
        <p>Four auto-renewing monthly Subscriptions are offered, each providing an Allowance of Units: Lite, 750 Units a month, $4.99 a month; Plus, 2,000 Units, $9.99; Pro, 4,500 Units, $19.99; and Max, 10,000 Units, $39.99. The figures in Units are the ones that govern. The page equivalents shown in the App — about 75, 200, 450 and 1,000 pages — assume a typical marked page at Brief output, so Detailed output uses an Allowance about three times faster and a scan containing pages the model only reads goes further. No plan is unlimited, and all use remains subject to section 9.</p>
        <p>The Allowance is made available for each calendar month in which your Subscription is active, and resets at 00:00 UTC on the first day of the month; Settings shows the next reset in your local time. The reset follows the calendar, not your billing date. An Allowance is capacity for one month, not a deposit: Units unspent at the reset do not carry into the next month. The one exception is an upgrade: if you move to a larger plan mid-month, Units already available under the smaller plan are carried over, and those carried Units expire at the next reset. When a Subscription ends, its Allowance and any carried Units end with it.</p>
        <p>A Top-Up is a separate, one-off purchase — currently 1,000 Units for $6.99. It does not renew. Its Units do not expire, they remain usable if a Subscription lapses or you never had one, and they are spent only after the Allowance or free grant and any carried Units are gone. Because a Top-Up is delivered immediately, Units once spent cannot be returned to you; section 15 governs refunds.</p>
        <p>Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of purchase. A Subscription renews automatically unless it is cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, and your Apple Account is charged for renewal within 24 hours before the current period ends. You can manage, change or cancel a Subscription at any time in Settings in the App, or in your Apple Account settings under Subscriptions. Cancelling stops the next renewal but does not end the period you have already paid for. Moving to a larger plan takes effect immediately; moving to a smaller one takes effect at the next renewal. Deleting the App does not cancel a Subscription. Any unused portion of a free trial period, where one is offered, is forfeited when a Subscription is purchased.</p>
        <h2 id="s14">14. Prices, taxes, and changes</h2>
        <p>Prices are shown in the App and on the App Store product page before purchase, in your local currency where Apple supports it. Prices stated in these Terms are in United States dollars and are indicative; the price shown by the App Store at the moment of purchase is the price that applies. Prices are inclusive or exclusive of tax according to Apple's rules for your storefront, and Apple collects and remits tax where it is required to. We may change prices for new purchases at any time. For an existing Subscription, a price increase does not take effect until Apple has given you notice in accordance with its rules and, where required, obtained your consent; if you do not consent, the Subscription does not renew.</p>
        <h2 id="s15">15. Refunds</h2>
        <p>Apple processes every purchase, and Apple handles every refund. We cannot issue, approve or decline a refund for an App Store purchase, and we never see your payment details. To request one, use Apple's Report a Problem page (<a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>) or contact Apple Support. Refunds are granted at Apple's discretion under its own policies and under any consumer rights you have that cannot be excluded by agreement. A refunded Subscription stops providing its Allowance. If you believe the App is defective, please also write to us at <a href="mailto:matdo@matdolab.com">matdo@matdolab.com</a>. We would rather fix the problem.</p>
        <h2 id="s16">16. Availability, updates, and support</h2>
        <p>We may release updates that add, change or remove features, including changes to how grading works or which model performs it. Whether an update installs automatically is governed by your Device settings. The Service depends on a third-party model provider and on the internet, and we do not commit to uninterrupted availability. We may cease publishing the App, or cease supporting a particular operating system version, on reasonable notice where notice is practicable. Support is provided by email at <a href="mailto:matdo@matdolab.com">matdo@matdolab.com</a>; we aim to respond promptly, but these Terms do not commit us to a defined response time or service level. Apple has no obligation to furnish support for the App.</p>
        <h2 id="s17">17. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>The App, its source code, design, interface, prompts, and the Matdo and Matdo Grade names and logos are owned by Matdo Lab LLC and protected by intellectual property law. These Terms grant you a licence to use the App and nothing more.</p>
        <p>Student Work is yours (or your students'). We claim no ownership of it and no licence to it beyond what is needed to return the Output to you. As between you and us, the Output is yours to use, keep and share. If you send us feedback or a feature suggestion, we may use it without obligation or payment to you; please do not send us anything you consider confidential, and never send us student work by email.</p>
        <h2 id="s18">18. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>The App is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title and non-infringement, and any warranty that the App will be uninterrupted, timely, secure or error-free. Without limiting section 5, we expressly disclaim any warranty as to the accuracy, reliability or fitness of the Output. Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of implied warranties, so some of the above may not apply to you. Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits a right you have under consumer protection law that cannot be excluded or limited by agreement.</p>
        <h2 id="s19">19. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Matdo Lab LLC is not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive damages, nor for lost profits, lost business, lost goodwill, lost or corrupted records, an incorrect grade or item of feedback, or any decision made from the Output, arising out of or relating to the App or these Terms, whether in contract, tort or otherwise, and whether or not we were advised of the possibility. To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total aggregate liability arising out of or relating to the App or these Terms is limited to the greatest of: the amounts you paid for the App in the twelve months preceding the event giving rise to the claim; the total amount you have paid for the App; or one hundred United States dollars. These limits apply even if a remedy fails of its essential purpose. Nothing in this section limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or for any other liability that cannot lawfully be limited. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so some of the above may not apply to you.</p>
        <h2 id="s20">20. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Matdo Lab LLC against any claim, loss or expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of your use of the App in breach of these Terms, your submission of Student Work without the permission described in section 10, or a decision you made from the Output in breach of section 5.</p>
        <h2 id="s21">21. Term and termination</h2>
        <p>These Terms apply from the moment you first use the App and continue until terminated. You may terminate at any time by cancelling any Subscription and deleting the App from your Devices. We may suspend or terminate your licence, or refuse grading requests, if you materially breach these Terms — in particular sections 9 and 10. Apple may terminate your licence under the Apple EULA on its own terms. Deleting the App deletes every saved grade on that Device with it; export anything you need to keep before you do. Sections 5, 11, 15 and 17 to 22 survive termination.</p>
